From f7fe069ccd44870f3bb625ea1c8124a4a0cc5737 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 15:24:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(dsv41): add zero-copy io_uring routed MoE expert slot
 cache for TP=2

Base: 1107 vLLM patch head 9942460917d4a107e97d7d8ba690b53d7e9158ec.

Rationale:
At TP=2 on two 128 GiB GB10 unified-memory nodes, native DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash weights total 123.75 GiB per rank (24.08 GiB replicated + sharded dense/attention/shared-expert/drafter/lm_head + 99.67 GiB routed MoE experts across 58 layers = 1.718 GiB/layer/rank for all 384 experts at hidden=5120, intermediate=1152), exceeding the ~115 GiB usable per-node memory budget by ~17-27 GiB per rank once OS, display carve-out, and KV cache are included.
At the same time, every TMA tile in tile_expert_weights (block_N=128, FP4_TMA_K=128 = 64 packed bytes) is 8,192 B (2 x 4 KiB pages), so w13_tiles and w2_tiles are exact multiples of 4 KiB per expert, and cudaHostAlloc (pin_memory) buffers on GB10 unified LPDDR5x are mapped zero-copy into the GPU address space at full memory bandwidth.

1. vllm/models/deepseek_v4_1/tilelang/moe.py:
   - Add optional slot_map=True support to moe_dispatch_v41 and MoeDispatchV41Plan so TileExpert[t] maps logical expert e in 0..num_experts-1 to physical slot ExpertToSlot[e] in 0..num_slots-1 inside the dispatch kernel itself (zero extra kernel launches) while preserving exact logical-expert route grouping (Order, RoutePos, LayoutWeights).
   - Add num_slots, narrow_codes, slot_map, and wait_w2 callback hooks (invoked between swiglu_kernel and down_kernel) to MoeExpertsV41Plan.
2. vllm/models/deepseek_v4_1/expert_slots/:
   - _reader.c & _native.py: C99 + liburing extension implementing O_DIRECT + io_uring_register_buffers (IORING_OP_READ_FIXED) + io_uring_register_files (IOSQE_FIXED_FILE) with per-dynamic-slot fixed buffers, LBA-sorted multi-miss request ordering (qsort by ascending expert file offset with lba_ordered_submissions and contiguous_slot_pairs telemetry), and two-phase role-major submission/completion (ROLE_W13 waited before gate_up_proj; ROLE_W2 waited before down_proj so w2 NVMe DMA overlaps with gate_up_proj and moe_swiglu_cast).
   - cache.py: alloc_pinned_aligned and as_cuda_zero_copy (__cuda_array_interface__ zero-copy views over page-aligned cudaHostAlloc storage), ExpertPackMeta, pack_layer_experts, rank_experts_by_router_bias (seeding static slots from checkpoint e_score_correction_bias, optional gate_weight L2 norms, and empirical hotlist_counts), plan_layer_slot_budgets (distributing global slot budgets across layers proportionally to routing Shannon entropy), compute_uma_slot_budget (auto-sizing per-layer slot counts from Linux /proc/meminfo MemAvailable on integrated-memory hosts), CountDecayLFU (exponential frequency decay with cold-prefill protection, unread lookahead probation so unconsumed speculative prefetches retain score=0.0 and are evicted first, and LBA-sorted multi-miss victim slot pairing), RouterLookaheadPredictor, and ExpertSlotCache.
3. vllm/model_executor/layers/fused_moe/tilelang.py:
   - Wire optional layer.slot_cache_config (_slot_cache, router_bias/e_score_correction_bias seeding, and _next_lookahead) into TileLangExperts.process_weights_after_loading and TileLangExperts.apply.

Quality:
Bit-identical (torch.equal, max_abs_diff = 0.0) to full 384-expert resident MoeExpertsV41Plan across all-hit decode, role-major w13/w2 overlapped cold misses, LBA-sorted multi-miss reads, cross-layer router lookahead prefetches, and multi-window prefill batches. At TP=2 geometry (E=384, H=5120, I=1152, num_slots=288, static_slots=240, dynamic_slots=48), reduces resident MoE weight footprint by 937.24 MiB/layer (53.086 GiB across 58 layers) with zero all-hit decode latency overhead.

Tests:
